r8genxpkg.f: do not write xpkg(4,4) when nx = 3.

xpkg is declared REAL*8 xpkg(nx,4). For evenly spaced x the routine writes
xpkg(4,4) only "if(nx.gt.3)" (the ialg flag lives there); for unevenly
spaced x it writes it unconditionally, which for nx = 3 is 8 bytes past the
end of the array. glibc hides this in malloc padding; the macOS allocator
traps at a later, unrelated allocation. PB3D hits it through
EZspline_setup1_r8 on mode ranges of exactly three radial points
(interp_V_spline), which produced the intermittent SIGTRAP crashes.
Found and verified with Guard Malloc, 8 October 2026 (PB3D issue #4).

--- a/pspline/r8genxpkg.f
+++ b/pspline/r8genxpkg.f
@@ -173,11 +173,13 @@
 c
       if(xpkg(1,4).ne.0.0_r8) then
          xpkg(1,4)=abs(ialg)
+         if(nx.gt.3) then
          if(ialg.lt.0) then
             xpkg(4,4)=1.0_r8  ! check init guess
          else
             xpkg(4,4)=0.0_r8
          endif
+         endif
 c
          if(abs(ialg).eq.3) then
 c
